\title{Reef Model Simulation & Results Plotting Functions}
\description{
This file contains plotting functions for visualizing results of
steady-state and dynamic simulations in mizerReef models. These
functions help users interpret model outputs, compare scenarios, and
analyze effects of parameter changes or management interventions.
Plots in this file focus on simulation results, time series, and
comparative analyses—not input parameter verification.
}
\details{
Functions in this file:
\itemize{
\item plotBiomass: Biomass of species groups and unstructured components
through time.
\item plotSpectra2: Two size spectra (e.g., models or scenarios) in one plot.
\item plotSpectraRelative: Relative or percent change between two spectra.
\item plotProductivity: Total productivity for each species group through
time or at steady state.
\item plotProductivityRelative: Relative or percent change in productivity
between two models or scenarios.
\item plot2Productivity: Productivity of two models or two size ranges in
one plot.
\item plotTotalAbundance: Total abundance for each species group at steady
state.
\item plotTotalBiomass: Total fishable biomass for each species group at
steady state.
\item plot2TotalBiomass: Total biomass of two models or two size ranges in
one plot.
\item plotTotalBiomassRelative: Relative change in total biomass between
two models or scenarios.
\item plotRelativeContribution: Relative contribution of each species group
to total abundance, biomass, and productivity.
\item plotRefugeDensity: Density of refuge through time for each group
(simulation output).
}

For each plot type, an interactive plotly version exists (e.g.,
plotlyBiomass, plotlyProductivity).

These tools are especially useful for:
\itemize{
\item Visualizing simulation results and time series
\item Comparing model scenarios, interventions, or parameter sets
\item Diagnosing unexpected model behavior or trends
\item Communicating model outcomes to stakeholders
}

For input parameter checking and setup, see plotting functions in
\code{reef-parameter-plots.R}.
}
